{
    "background_story": "Zariah was a brilliant and reclusive botanist who spent most of her life studying the rare and exotic colchicum flower. She became fascinated with its unique properties and potential medicinal applications. Zariah's obsession with the colchicum led her to travel to remote regions of the world, often putting herself in harm's way to collect specimens. Her tireless efforts eventually led to a groundbreaking discovery, as she isolated a compound from the flower that showed great promise in treating a debilitating disease. Zariah's findings were met with international acclaim, and she was hailed as a pioneer in her field. Despite her newfound fame, she remained humble and dedicated to her work, continuing to study the colchicum and unlock its secrets.",
